<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	18.07	    - 84	    18.05     18.10</p>
<p>91-Day	20.31	    - 48	    20.18     20.40</p>
<p>181-Day     21.41	    - 44	    21.37     21.47</p>
<p>350-Day     22.74				22.69     22.78</p>
<p>Last week the 357-day paper was assigned at 23.06 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.28 bln pesos	2.85</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   2.89 bln pesos	3.61</p>
<p>181-Day     800 million pesos   4.26 bln pesos	5.33</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   2.21 bln pesos	3.68</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.88 on demand of 11.65 billion pesos compared with 4.33 the week before, on demand of 12.99 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    3 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    9 basis points</p>
<p>    181-Day			   6 basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			   4 basis points</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
